  "section_notes": "The 7% permanent test-failure cap (above the 5% benchmark) with no sales stop is the main weakening and clearly benefits Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). The recall trigger of 8 per 100,000 is mandatory with no interim allowance, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), while the 24-month new-unit shut-off delay and 60-month retrofit window favour Northwind, whose installed base is only 38% shut-off capable. Suppression at 36 months is within the acceptable range and eases Halcyon's per-unit cost burden."
